  m_Name: PY_RUN_11_LOOPS_SUM
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.QuestionData
  id: PY_RUN_11_LOOPS_SUM
  language: 1
  topic: Loops
  difficulty: 1
  questionType: 2
  questionText: This loop should add up the numbers from 1 to n. Fill in the line
    that adds i to total on every turn.
  code: "total = 0\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    ____\nprint(total)"
  answerFormat: 2
  choices: []
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 0
  acceptedAnswers: []
  caseSensitive: 1
  referenceFill: total = total + i
  runTests:
  - setup: n = 3
    expectedOutput: 6
  - setup: n = 5
    expectedOutput: 15
  - setup: n = 1
    expectedOutput: 1
  explanation: Each turn of the loop gives i the next number. total = total + i adds
    it to the running total, so n = 3 gives 1 + 2 + 3 = 6.
  hint: total must remember its old value and add i to it.
  wrongChoiceFeedback: []
  wrongAnswerFeedback: The line must change total using total itself and i. Make
    sure it is inside the loop (it is already indented for you).
